<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is T.J. McConnell Worth $11m to the Pacers?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>McConnell is paid <strong>$11m</strong> because he is one of the most effective reserve guards in the league and Indiana has built a role around exactly what he does.</p>
<ul>
<li>He led the league in steals per 36 minutes in several seasons and plays a pressing style few guards can.</li>
<li>He went undrafted in 2015 and his first contract paid <strong>$4.47m</strong> across four years.</li>
<li>He turned 34 in March, which is why the last year of this deal is a club option.</li>
<li>He has never started regularly at Indiana and the pay reflects a reserve role.</li>
<li>Only <strong>$26.2m</strong> of the <strong>$44.8m</strong> is guaranteed, so the club keeps the choice.</li>
</ul>
<p>He has been at Indiana for eight seasons, longer than any other player on the roster.</p>

