<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/tj-mcconnell/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/tj-mcconnell/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is T.J. McConnell’s Salary in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"McConnell earns $11m in 2026-27, level with Nesmith as the sixth largest salary on the Indiana payroll. It rises from $10.2m last season. His career earnings reach $66.27m across twelve seasons. The salary is 5.33% of the club’s $206.30m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for T.J. McConnell Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Two seasons remain after this one. The first is worth about $11.8m and the second is a club option with a deadline of June 29, 2028. He turns 35 in March."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does T.J. McConnell Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $11m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Is T.J. McConnell’s Contract Worth at Indiana?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"McConnell signed a four-year extension worth $44.8m with Indiana on September 3, 2024, of which $26.2m is guaranteed. The final season is a club option with a deadline of June 29, 2028. If Indiana exercises it, $5m is guaranteed straight away and the rest on the day of the 2028 draft’s second round."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is T.J. McConnell’s Net Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"McConnell’s net worth is estimated at around $26.5m, taken from his $66.27m in career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for him. He played two seasons at Duquesne and two at Arizona, went undrafted in 2015, and was paid $525k in his first NBA season. He has since earned more than $66m without ever being drafted or selected as an All-Star."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Is T.J. McConnell Worth $11m to the Pacers?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"McConnell is paid $11m because he is one of the most effective reserve guards in the league and Indiana has built a role around exactly what he does. He has been at Indiana for eight seasons, longer than any other player on the roster."}}]}</script>
